  "_doc": "The real night sky for the star look 'real' (shaders/atmosphere.hlsli realStars; engine/render/StarSky.h): the brightest stars with their J2000 position (ra = right ascension in hours, dec = declination in degrees), visual magnitude and B-V colour, written from the Bright Star Catalogue (values to the tenth; a few arc minutes off at worst). They are the constellations as they are: Orion, Crux, Scorpius, Sagittarius, Centaurus, Carina, Ursa Major, Cassiopeia, Cygnus, Lyra, Aquila, Leo, Gemini, Taurus with the Pleiades and Hyades, Canis Major, Perseus, Auriga, Pegasus, Andromeda, Bootes, Virgo, Corvus, Grus, Eridanus... The observer stands at `latitude` (the Southern Cross and the galactic centre high, Orion and the Great Bear still seen); the sky turns with the hour (sidereal: `lstAtMidnight` = the local sidereal time at 0 h, hours). `clouds` = the two Magellanic Clouds (ra, dec, radius in degrees, brightness).",
